# section convert.nativeTextFormatters

# rationale: Native, allocation-free Int64 -> decimal text into a caller-owned
#   scratch buffer. convertSignedInt64ToString has a SemanticScript body and so
#   does NOT link in native/webServer builds (SSCG002), which forced apps onto
#   c.snprintf (format-string crash risk) or reading integer columns as SQL TEXT.
#   This delegates to a runtimeBinding shim, so it links in those builds.
# invariant: Returns the scratch pointer on success; null when capacity is too
#   small. A truncated number is a wrong number, so it fails closed rather than
#   returning partial text.
operation formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer
input operation formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer inputValue Int64
input operation formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer scratch OpaquePointer
input operation formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer capacity Int32
output operation formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer String
effect formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer write memory.buffer
memory formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer heap no
async formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer no
useCapability formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer conversionMemoryBufferWriteCapability
operationBody formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer runtimeBinding
purpose operation formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer "Format an Int64 as null-terminated decimal text into the caller-provided scratch buffer; returns the buffer, or null if capacity is insufficient."
invariant operation formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer "Returns the scratch pointer on success, or null when capacity is too small; a 64-bit decimal needs up to 21 bytes (sign + 19 digits + NUL); never overflows the buffer."
warning formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer "A null return means the buffer was too small - the caller must check before using the result as a String."
runtimeBindingPrecondition formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer "scratch points to at least capacity writable bytes."
runtimeBinding formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer native.ss_convert_int64_to_string

# rationale: Native, allocation-free Float64 -> shortest round-trippable decimal
#   text into a caller-owned scratch buffer. The native sibling of
#   formatSignedInt64IntoBuffer for doubles; links in native/webServer builds
#   where convertFloat64ToString (a SemanticScript body) does not.
# invariant: Emits the shortest decimal that round-trips to the same double
#   (0.1 -> "0.1"); returns null when capacity is too small.
operation formatFloat64IntoBuffer
input operation formatFloat64IntoBuffer inputValue Float64
input operation formatFloat64IntoBuffer scratch OpaquePointer
input operation formatFloat64IntoBuffer capacity Int32
output operation formatFloat64IntoBuffer String
effect formatFloat64IntoBuffer write memory.buffer
memory formatFloat64IntoBuffer heap no
async formatFloat64IntoBuffer no
useCapability formatFloat64IntoBuffer conversionMemoryBufferWriteCapability
operationBody formatFloat64IntoBuffer runtimeBinding
purpose operation formatFloat64IntoBuffer "Format a Float64 as the shortest null-terminated decimal text that round-trips to the same value, into the caller-provided scratch buffer; returns the buffer, or null if capacity is insufficient."
invariant operation formatFloat64IntoBuffer "Emits the shortest decimal that round-trips to the input double; non-finite inputs render as nan/inf/-inf; returns null when capacity is too small; never overflows the buffer."
warning formatFloat64IntoBuffer "A null return means the buffer was too small - the caller must check before using the result as a String."
runtimeBindingPrecondition formatFloat64IntoBuffer "scratch points to at least capacity writable bytes."
runtimeBinding formatFloat64IntoBuffer native.ss_convert_float64_to_string

